  "question": {
    "text": "A parallel beam of monochromatic light of wavelength $600 \\mathrm{~nm}$ passes through single slit of $0.4 \\mathrm{~mm}$ width. Angular divergence corresponding to second order minima would be ______ $\\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{rad}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\sin \\theta \\simeq \\theta \\simeq \\frac{2 \\lambda}{b}$\n$=\\frac{2 \\times 600 \\times 10^{-9}}{4 \\times 10^{-4}}=3 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{rad}$\nTotal divergence $=(3+3) \\times 10^{-3}=6 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{rad}$"
  }
}